Honestly, I think {jbeplibu to se smuni lodu'u ko'a jbena fi'o plibu ko'e
toi} would've been enough. Also, including nakni and fetsi at least
implicitly restricts it to (some combination of) two genders- that is, that
while a person can be, for example, XX, XY, X, XXY, XYY, etc., they can't
be XT, to make up a gender gene.


